From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:41:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Compare the start of a UTF-8 sequence as a size_t

Utf8Proc::Analyze() walks the string with a size_t index and keeps the
start of the current sequence as an int, and the rewind after a bad
continuation byte compares the two, which -Wsign-compare reports. The
start is a position in the same string, taken from the index, so it
is compared as a size_t.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
 src/duckdb/third_party/utf8proc/utf8proc_wrapper.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/duckdb/third_party/utf8proc/utf8proc_wrapper.cpp b/src/duckdb/third_party/utf8proc/utf8proc_wrapper.cpp
index 6d046d1120..9315bce262 100644
--- a/src/duckdb/third_party/utf8proc/utf8proc_wrapper.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/third_party/utf8proc/utf8proc_wrapper.cpp
@@ -210,7 +210,7 @@ std::string Utf8Proc::RemoveInvalid(const char *s, size_t len) {
 			// A bad continuation byte (not a truncated tail, not a bad codepoint after a fully well-formed sequence) 
 			// means the byte at invalid_pos was never actually consumed as part of this sequence 
 			// rewind so it gets reprocessed on its own next iteration
-			if (invalid_reason == UnicodeInvalidReason::BYTE_MISMATCH && i > first_pos_seq) {
+			if (invalid_reason == UnicodeInvalidReason::BYTE_MISMATCH && i > static_cast<size_t>(first_pos_seq)) {
 				i = invalid_pos - 1;
 			}
 			continue;
